: proto.rk1 -- the on-target source tree, on its OWN filesystem.  Written
: rather than arrived at, like proto: every source the target can rebuild
: is named below, and nothing is withheld from it.
:
: The rk driver maps unit N to block N*NRKBLK (4872) of the one IDE disk,
: so this is unix.img at offset 4872 and needs no second file.  It moved
: off rk0 because /src is 1814 blocks and rk0 had 607 left -- too few for
: the on-target floppy build, which writes a 720-block image.  Mount it with
:     mount /dev/rk1 /src
: rk0 keeps an empty /src as the mount point.
:
: /src/sys/BOOT.COM is not carried either: $KBIN is what MKKBIN builds on
: the reader's DOS -- the kernel, the boot sector, the layout golden -- the
: way $BIN is what MKBIN builds.
:
: No boot sector ('-'): nothing here is booted, and neither is rk0.
: fsize 4800 + swap 0 fits the 4872 blocks the driver gives one unit;
: swap stays on rk0, where the kernel's swplo=4000/nswap=872 puts it.
-
4800 100 0
d--777 0 0
: /src -- ALL source that can be rebuilt on the target, in four directories:
:
:   rt/      the V6 runtime, built ONCE and shared (mkrt).  desmet/ and usr/
:            link it as ../rt/NAME with -L../rt/ for CSTDIO.S; sys/ takes
:            only the library, for the long-arithmetic helpers.
:   desmet/  the DeSmet toolchain itself + the three image tools (mkall)
:   sys/     the RealXV6 kernel, in its own KEN/ DMR/ H/ split (mkkern),
:            then the boot floppy that carries it (mkimg)
:   usr/     the DeSmet-built user programs (mkusr)
:
: The bulky sources are read straight from where they are developed, via the
: $BUILD / $RT / $KERNEL tokens, so nothing is duplicated into the tracked
: image tree; only the build scripts and BIND response files live under
: image/usr/dsrc.
:
: C88's include search is dead here (V6MISC's _MSDOS2_ is 0, so findfile()
: never runs and C88 just open()s the name it was handed, which DCOMPAT
: resolves case-blind), so anything outside the cwd is reached by spelling
: the path: C88's -i prefix for headers (options come AFTER the file name),
: a path'd source name for a compile, and BIND's -L / an explicit .O for a
: link.  That is enough to keep sys/ split the way drive_c\XV6\KERNEL is --
: mkkern runs in sys/ and compiles KEN/NAME and DMR/NAME with -iH/, since
: no cwd would make C88 find H/ by itself.  Case is what fixes the spelling
: of these directories:
:   - KEN/ DMR/ H/ are UPPER, because C88 upper-cases the source name when
:     it chains to GEN (C88.C: nextpgm[nopt++]=toupper(*cur++)), and the .O
:     that ASM88 then creat()s under that name gets no case fold at all --
:     creat() is a bare syscall in DCOMPAT.C.  A lower-case ken/ would be
:     compiled from and written to a directory that does not exist.
:   - <os.h> stays lower-case in the source, so -iH/ makes "H/os.h" and
:     DCOMPAT's UPPER fold turns the whole path into H/OS.H -- which works
:     only because the H is already upper.
:   - rt/ is lower-case for the mirror-image reason: every source spells it
:     "UNIX.H" in UPPER, so ../rt/UNIX.H hits VERBATIM and the fold never
:     runs -- it could not help there, since foldcase() rewrites the whole
:     path and would turn ../rt/ into ../RT/.
rt      d--777 0 0
        UNIX.H      ---644 0 0 $RT/UNIX.H
        CRT0.A      ---644 0 0 $RT/CRT0.A
        DCRT0.A     ---644 0 0 $RT/DCRT0.A
        V6MISC.A    ---644 0 0 $RT/V6MISC.A
        SETEXIT.A   ---644 0 0 $RT/SETEXIT.A
        SYSCALL.C   ---644 0 0 $RT/SYSCALL.C
        USTR.C      ---644 0 0 $RT/USTR.C
        PRINTF.C    ---644 0 0 $RT/PRINTF.C
        DCOMPAT.C   ---644 0 0 $RT/DCOMPAT.C
        V6DOS.C     ---644 0 0 $RT/V6DOS.C
        V6CHAIN.C   ---644 0 0 $RT/V6CHAIN.C
        ULIB.C      ---644 0 0 $RT/ULIB.C
        UCOMPAT.C   ---644 0 0 $RT/UCOMPAT.C
        CTIME.C     ---644 0 0 $RT/CTIME.C
        CSTDIO.S    ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/DESMET/LIB/CSTDIO.S
        mkrt        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKRT
        $
desmet  d--777 0 0
        mkall       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKALL
        GENL        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/GENL
        C88L        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/C88L
        ASML        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/ASML
        BINDL       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/BINDL
        LIBL        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/LIBL
        D2AL        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/D2AL
        E2CL        ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/E2CL
        MKBOOTL     ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKBOOTL
        OBJ.H       ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/OBJ.H
        NODES.H     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/NODES.H
        PASS1.H     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/PASS1.H
        PASS2.H     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/PASS2.H
        INST86.H    ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/INST86.H
        ASM88.H     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM88.H
        GEN.C       ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN.C
        GEN2.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN2.C
        GEN3.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN3.C
        GEN4.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN4.C
        GEN5.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN5.C
        GEN6.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/GEN/GEN6.C
        C88.C       ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C88.C
        C2.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C2.C
        C3.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C3.C
        C4.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C4.C
        C5.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C5.C
        C6.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C6.C
        C7.C        ---644 0 0 $BUILD/C88/C7.C
        ASM88.C     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM88.C
        ASM2.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM2.C
        ASM3.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM3.C
        ASM4.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM4.C
        ASM5.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/ASM/ASM5.C
        BIND.C      ---644 0 0 $BUILD/BIND/BIND.C
        LIB88.C     ---644 0 0 $BUILD/LIB88/LIB88.C
        D2A.C       ---644 0 0 $RT/D2A.C
        E2C.C       ---644 0 0 $RT/E2C.C
        MKBOOT.C    ---644 0 0 $RT/MKBOOT.C
        $
sys     d--777 0 0
        mkkern      ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKKERN
        KERNL       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/KERNL
        BOOTL       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/BOOTL
        mkimg       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKIMG
        selfboot    ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/SELFBOOT
        banner.ed   ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/BANNER.ED
        BOOT.COM    ---644 0 0 $KBIN/BOOT.COM
        BOOT    d--777 0 0
                BOOTSEC.A   ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/BOOT/BOOTSEC.A
                $
        KEN     d--777 0 0
                ALLOC.C     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/ALLOC.C
                CLOCK.C     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/CLOCK.C
                FIO.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/FIO.C
                IGET.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/IGET.C
                MAIN.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/MAIN.C
                MALLOC.C    ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/MALLOC.C
                NAMI.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/NAMI.C
                PIPE.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/PIPE.C
                PRF.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/PRF.C
                RDWRI.C     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/RDWRI.C
                SIG.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SIG.C
                SLP.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SLP.C
                SUBR.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SUBR.C
                SYS1.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SYS1.C
                SYS2.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SYS2.C
                SYS3.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SYS3.C
                SYS4.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SYS4.C
                SYSENT.C    ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/SYSENT.C
                TEXT.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/TEXT.C
                TRAP.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/KEN/TRAP.C
                $
        DMR     d--777 0 0
                BIO.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/BIO.C
                FD.C        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/FD.C
                IDE.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/IDE.C
                KBD.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/KBD.C
                KL.C        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/KL.C
                MEM.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/MEM.C
                PC.C        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/PC.C
                RK.C        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/RK.C
                TTY.C       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/TTY.C
                UART.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/UART.C
                DPAD.C      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/DPAD.C
                DPAD2.C     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/DPAD2.C
                M86.A       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/M86.A
                CPAD.A      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/CPAD.A
                ZEND.A      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/DMR/ZEND.A
                $
        H       d--777 0 0
                BUF.H       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/BUF.H
                CONF.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/CONF.H
                EXEC.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/EXEC.H
                FILE.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/FILE.H
                FILSYS.H    ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/FILSYS.H
                INO.H       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/INO.H
                INODE.H     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/INODE.H
                OS.H        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/OS.H
                PARAM.H     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/PARAM.H
                PC.H        ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/PC.H
                PROC.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/PROC.H
                REG.H       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/REG.H
                SYSTM.H     ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/SYSTM.H
                TEXT.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/TEXT.H
                TTY.H       ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/TTY.H
                USER.H      ---644 0 0 $KERNEL/H/USER.H
                $
        $
usr     d--777 0 0
        mkusr       ---644 0 0 ../usr/dsrc/MKUSR
        INIT.C      ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/INIT.C
        CAT.C       ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/CAT.C
        CHMOD.C     ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/CHMOD.C
        CP.C        ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/CP.C
        DATE.C      ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/DATE.C
        ECHO.C      ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/ECHO.C
        ED.C        ---644 0 0 ../../drive_c/XV6/USR/ED.C
